  "caption_final": "Ramayana has crossed ₹900 crore net at the Indian box office, trade tracker Sacnilk estimates: ₹906.90 crore in 17 days, after ₹27.40 crore on Saturday, 21 November. By the same count, its worldwide gross is now ₹1,616.70 crore.\n\nOn Sacnilk's list, only three Indian films had passed ₹900 crore net in India before it: Pushpa 2 (in 11 days), Dhurandhar 2 (14 days) and Baahubali 2 (19 days). At 17 days, Ramayana is the third-fastest to the mark.\n\nTrackers count differently: Bollywood Hungama's total is lower, and the makers haven't announced a figure.\n\nHave you watched Ramayana in a theatre yet?\n\nSources: Sacnilk, The Week, Filmibeat, Bollywood Hungama\n\n#Ramayana #RamayanaPart1 #BoxOffice #IndianCinema #idlynerd\n\nImage: World Of Ramayana (official trailer)",
